     "importedLaw": "Keyed by the registry relations[].observationAddressSelector. A representable imported row can establish a known match: exists true, none false, count-at-most false above N. The fixture cannot represent wrapper completeness, observation window or population, selection completeness or staleness, so absence of a matching row never proves absence: exists is never false and none, count-at-most and all-covered are never true. An atom of an unrepresentable selector is unknown. Unobservable, unmapped or observability-absent runtime rows are unknown, never unhit.",
     "nativeLaw": "Native relations follow the atom owner's strong Kleene quantifiers over the supplied facts with the case's declared Coverage: complete Coverage lets absence decide; partial or unknown Coverage, or any unknown match, leaves exists false, none true, count-at-most true and all-covered true unknown.",
-    "ruleLaw": "Required evidence absent from evidenceAvailable makes the rule unknown for every enumerated subject. Optional evidence absent with complete Coverage is the disclosed non-gating IMPORT.ABSENT_FOR_PREDICATE case when it is the only unknown cause. Every other unknown rule result for an enumerated subject lists the rule in CaseResult.indeterminateRules; an enabled gating rule at the policy threshold makes the observed verdict indeterminate unless a live unwaived gating finding makes it fail.",
+    "ruleLaw": "Every enumerated subject is evaluated whatever the evidence (composition contract sections 5 and 9.5). A known true root emits its finding, waived or live. A declared required evidence kind absent from evidenceAvailable is a rule-level deficiency independent of the root value: the rule is listed in CaseResult.indeterminateRules and every enumerated subject without a known finding stays unknown (a known false root is not an authoritative no-match), with no subject the rule is still listed. An unknown root lists the rule too unless its only causes are absent optional evidence, which is the disclosed non-blocking IMPORT.ABSENT_FOR_PREDICATE case; an incomplete-Coverage or uncertain native match, a required kind and a fixture representation limit are blocking causes. A live unwaived finding of an enabled gating rule at the policy threshold makes the observed verdict fail; otherwise a listed gating rule makes it indeterminate; a non-gating rule never changes the verdict beyond advisory.",
     "expectationLaw": "finding: known matching findings above maxCount is unmet; at least minCount is met unless maxCount is present and an enumerated subject (within subjects when given) is unknown for the rule, which is indeterminate; below minCount is indeterminate when such an unknown subject exists, otherwise unmet. no-finding: a known finding is unmet; otherwise an unknown subject is indeterminate; otherwise met. verdict: met exactly when the observed verdict equals it. indeterminate: met exactly when the rule is in indeterminateRules. A case is failed with any unmet, else indeterminate with any indeterminate, else passed.",
     "resultLimit": "PolicyTestResultV1 and CaseResult are unchanged: indeterminateRules and expectationOutcomes name the affected rules and expectations but carry no per-rule unknown cause (Coverage, missing evidence or fixture representation)."
